<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠρίων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Orion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.121
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.310
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				572
			</span></i>, Telesarch. ap. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.262
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.2.12
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> the
				<i>constellation</i> named after him, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.486
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				488
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.274
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				598
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				609
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				361b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				941b24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> a fabulous
			Indian bird, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				15.1.69
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				17.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				26.202
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span>
			
				Att.
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1153
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				213
			</span></i>, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Theod.</u>
				1.272
			</span></i> H.: we also find <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠᾰρίων</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Corinn.
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				2.77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				265
			</span></i>, and in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀαρίωνα</span>
			); Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠαριώνειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>I.</u>
					4(3).49(67)
				</span></i>
			; the Homeric <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠρῑων</span> arose
			by contraction of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠα-</span> and metrical
			lengthening of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι.</span>]</div>
